# Flutter Conventions

## UI Framework

- Material Design 3 only — no deprecated Material 2 APIs
- `StatelessWidget` first
- `StatefulWidget` only for local ephemeral state (form controllers, scroll controllers, animation controllers)

## State Management

- `flutter_bloc` only — BLoC class for feature logic
- Cubit only for pure UI state with **no network calls** (e.g. `OtpUiCubit`)
- No Provider, Riverpod, GetX, or `setState` for feature/network logic
- `HydratedBloc` only for persistence-required state (theme, locale)

## Navigation

- GoRouter only: `context.go()`, `context.push()`, `context.pop()`
- Never `Navigator.push()` or `Navigator.pushNamed()` directly

## Networking

- Dio via `sl<ApiClientImpl>()` — never instantiate `Dio` in features
- Return type: `TaskEither<Failure, T>` — never `Future<T>` in repositories

## Dependency Injection

- GetIt (`sl`) — register in `di/` files
- Never call `sl<T>()` inside a widget constructor
- BLoCs registered as factories; repos/use cases as lazy singletons

## Localization

- Never hardcode UI strings — always `'key'.tr()`
- Arabic (`ar-AR`) is the default locale — design RTL first

## Responsive Layout

- `ScreenUtilInit` at app root (design size 360×800)
- Use `AppSpacing`, `AppDimension` — never `.w` / `.h` on primitives
- Fonts via `AppFont` / `AppFontArabic` only
